abstract: >-
  torch-dae is a generic framework that provides an AI skill-based workflow for
  evidence-grounded onboarding and integration of audio embedding models. It keeps
  model-specific dependencies in isolated environments and records provenance,
  checkpoint identity, environment resolution, public wrapper behavior, embeddings,
  and runtime verification as explicit artifacts. Research activities were mainly
  funded under the Ministerial Decree (DM) 118/2023, Mission 4, Component 1,
  Investment 4.1 of the National Recovery and Resilience Plan (PNRR) – “PNRR
  Research” – CUP: E11I23000100001.
